# MES2L676-100HP board clock = the core board's single-ended 27 MHz oscillator (U11),
# routed to FPGA_GCLK_27M on pin D18. It is the only system clock input; the core
# board's second oscillator is 125 MHz differential and feeds the DDR3 reference only.
# Official evidence (see the project validation archive):
#   * 教程1_硬件实验指导手册_盘古676系列100Pro+开发板.pdf, 2.1.2.2.3.2 「27MHz 单端时钟」:
#     U11 oscillator, table row "FPGA_GCLK_27M | FPGA 输入全局时钟 | D18";
#     125MHz differential (U7) "用于 DDR3 的参考时钟输入".
#   * 教程2_通用实验指导手册_盘古676系列100Pro+开发板.pdf, 7.3 接口列表 (MES2L676-100HP):
#     "clk input 1 系统时钟，27MHZ"; 7.2 "在 100K 板卡上单端时钟有一个 27MHZ 的时钟。
#     所以其周期约为 37.037ns。"
#   * Official demo 2_8_uart_test/source/uart_top.v: parameter BPS_NUM = 16'd234 (= 27e6/115200),
#     i.e. the vendor demo is built for the 27 MHz board clock.
# 27 MHz -> period 37.037 ns. The old 20 ns (50 MHz) constraint was an OVER-CONSTRAINT, not
# this board's clock: the same RTL met it with +5.219 ns setup slack (equivalent Fmax ~67.6 MHz).
# That run is kept as frequency-margin evidence only (see
# the project validation archive and the 50 MHz over-constraint experiment FDC
# pango_native_50mhz_overconstraint.fdc). The delivered constraint must describe the real board.
create_clock -name clk -period 37.037 -waveform {0 18.5185} [get_ports {clk}]
# 100 ps guard band on the board clock (stricter, not a relaxation) -- see the
# scope note above before comparing any slack value with earlier reports.
set_clock_uncertainty {0.100} [get_clocks {clk}] -setup -hold
# Hold margin (2026-10-19, CHANGE OF SCOPE - READ THIS BEFORE COMPARING NUMBERS):
# The delivered RTL used to close 27 MHz with only +0.011..+0.018 ns of hold slack, which
# made every performance change impossible: eight independent experiments (larger I-cache,
# store posting, order guard, ...) were rejected purely because they pushed hold negative
# (-1 .. -28 ps) even when their functional evidence was complete.
# This file therefore now declares a REAL GUARD BAND on the board clock:
#     set_clock_uncertainty {0.100} [get_clocks {clk}] -setup -hold
# A guard band makes the timing checks STRICTER (it is subtracted from slack); nothing is
# relaxed and the 27 MHz board clock itself is unchanged.
# => Consequence for the report: any slack printed from this point on is
#    "slack with a 100 ps guard band" and must NOT be compared with the pre-2026-10-19
#    numbers (+15.374/+0.018) that had no guard band. Both must be quoted with their scope.
# The router-side hold optimisation is still requested by build.tcl as well
#   pnr -fix_hold_violation_threshold 500 -fix_hold_violation_threshold_for_clk_tree 200 \
#       -fix_hold_violation_threshold_for_clock_path_cross_srb 200 -fix_hold_violation_iterations 2000
# (the option takes integer PICOSECONDS).
# KEY0/KEY1/UART are asynchronous board signals, not synchronous bus inputs.
# No blanket timing exception is applied to internal reset or AXI paths.
# Review synchronizer placement and asynchronous input paths after mapping.
